1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,600
Guru Nanak says: if you would play the game of love, come with your head on your palm.

2
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:13,700
Oregon, America. Sohan Singh Bhakna, a farmer from Punjab, hauls lumber in a sawmill.

3
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:21,000
Here he is taunted: you are a man from a slave country. That wound becomes his fire.

4
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:28,512
In 1913 the workers found the Ghadar Party, and choose him as its first president.

5
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:36,400
He bows before no idol. His head bows only to the Guru's word: stand firm against tyranny.

6
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:42,300
Baba Kesar Singh had taught him: live not for yourself, but for others.

7
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:51,419
1914. War breaks out, and he leaves everything and boards a ship for home. His head on his palm.

8
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:57,881
At Calcutta the British are waiting. He is arrested the moment he steps off the ship.

9
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:04,900
First a death sentence, then life. Sixteen years in prison, and his head never bowed.

10
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:12,166
He lived to see India free. This is sacrifice: to give your head, but never to bow it.
